---
import {getCollection} from 'astro:content';import SiteLayout from '../layouts/SiteLayout.astro';import {url} from '../lib/paths';
const lessons=(await getCollection('lessons')).sort((a,b)=>a.data.order-b.data.order);
const revision=lessons.filter(l=>l.data.advanced||['generics','concurrency','jvm','diagnostics','collections'].includes(l.data.module));
---
<SiteLayout title="Learning paths" summary="Choose a complete sequence or a focused revision route. Both use the same chapters and examples."><h2>Complete Java path</h2><p>Begin with compilation and types, then build through objects, generics and collections before studying concurrency and runtime behavior. Follow the previous/next controls in each lesson. Check prerequisites before skipping ahead.</p>{lessons.map((l,i)=><a class="lesson-row" href={url('learn/'+l.id+'/')}><span><strong>{String(i+1).padStart(2,'0')} · {l.data.title}</strong><small>{l.data.summary}</small></span></a>)}<h2>Experienced-developer revision</h2><p>Use the concept questions and exercises to identify gaps. Concentrate on equality, generics, collection behavior, concurrency correctness and JVM diagnostics. Return to prerequisites whenever an explanation depends on unfamiliar terminology.</p>{revision.map(l=><a class="lesson-row" href={url('learn/'+l.id+'/')}><span><strong>{l.data.title}</strong><small>{l.data.summary}</small></span></a>)}</SiteLayout>
